@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/grants/{grant_id}/revoke/prepare + /send — delivery-only revocation
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Grantor" as Grantor #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.revokeGrant(grantId)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Grantor -> SDK : revokeGrant(grantId)

group Phase 1 — prepare (no body; deploys nothing)
SDK -> API : POST .../grants/{grant_id}/revoke/prepare
API -> Domain : prepare revocation
Domain -> Chain : getGrant(grant_id) — fail fast on absence
alt no grant record
Domain --> API : 404 {code: grant_not_found}
else grant exists (revoked or not)
Domain --> API : RevokeGrantResp { contract }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end
end

group Sign and send
SDK -> SDK : sign locally with the grantor's wallet key
SDK -> API : POST .../grants/{grant_id}/revoke/send\n{ prepare_request: grant_id, echo, signed, token }
API -> Domain : deploy signed revokeGrant
Domain -> Chain : deploy
note right of Chain #FFF0C7
Grantor-only, idempotent: revoking a revoked
grant re-acknowledges instead of aborting.
Any other signer aborts
"grant revocation requires the grantor".
end note
alt clause aborts
Chain --> Domain : deploy errored
Domain -> Chain : re-read the record to name the cause
alt record absent
Domain --> API : 404 {code: grant_not_found}
else surviving unrevoked record
Domain --> API : 403 {code: grant_unauthorized}\n(the signer is not the grantor)
end
else clause lands
Chain --> Domain : finalized; acknowledged
Domain -> Chain : revocation readback: disclosure authority\nmust be observably cut before the\ngrantor is told it is
Domain --> API : deploy id
API --> SDK : 200 SendResp { deployId }
end
end

note over API, Chain #FFF0C7
Delivery-only for in-flight runs: they complete for their
owner, while the grantee's reveal and command claims fail
from the moment of revocation. The grantor keeps cancel
through the ordinary command envelope.
end note
@enduml
